<section class="brand-lab__section" id="brand-copy" aria-labelledby="brand-copy-title">
      <div class="brand-lab__section-heading">
        <p class="brand-lab__index">14 / Copy</p>
        <div><BrandHeading level={2} role="h3" id="brand-copy-title">Reusable strings</BrandHeading><p>Stop rewriting the same microcopy. These are the default forms for actions, states, and dates.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="brand-lab__copy-grid">
        <article>
          <span>Actions</span>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Inspect the workflow</dt><dd>Verb plus object. Never “Learn more” or “Click here.”</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Read the evidence</dt><dd>Names what the reader receives, not the interaction.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Book a working session</dt><dd>Commitment is explicit before the click.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Errors</span>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>What happened</dt><dd>“The file was not attached.”</dd></div>
            <div><dt>What is safe</dt><dd>“Your draft is safe.”</dd></div>
            <div><dt>What to do</dt><dd>“Attach a source or mark the claim Open.”</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Empty and loading</span>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Empty</dt><dd>Name the missing thing and the one action that fills it.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Loading</dt><dd>“Checking output” beats a bare spinner.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Partial</dt><dd>Say which part is verified and which is still open.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Dates and numbers</span>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Dates</dt><dd><code>2026-07-28</code> in metadata; “28 July 2026” in prose.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Ranges</dt><dd>State the window, not a vague “recently.”</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Metrics</dt><dd>Every number carries a source or it is not published.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="brand-lab__section" id="brand-inventory" aria-labelledby="brand-inventory-title">
      <div class="brand-lab__section-heading">
        <p class="brand-lab__index">15 / Inventory</p>
        <div><BrandHeading level={2} role="h3" id="brand-inventory-title">What already exists</BrandHeading><p>Reach for an existing module before writing new markup. Each entry names the file that owns the behavior.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="brand-lab__inventory">
        <article>
          <h3>Layouts</h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt><code>BaseLayout</code></dt><dd>Document shell: head, skip link, one <code>&lt;main&gt;</code>, header, footer, nav script.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>CommercialLayout</code></dt><dd>Service or standard page: shell plus entity graph and breadcrumbs.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>CaseStudyLayout</code></dt><dd>Article page: shell plus Article graph and dynamic params.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>SeoHead</code></dt><dd>Canonical metadata, robots policy, social cards, and discovery links.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>SiteHeader</code> · <code>SiteFooter</code> · <code>MotionEnhancement</code></dt><dd>Shared landmarks and the shell’s single progressive-enhancement script.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Content components</h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt><code>EvidenceNote</code></dt><dd>Attaches a claim to its verified source.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>Byline</code></dt><dd>Validated single-author signal rendered on editorial entries.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>FreshnessNotice</code></dt><dd>Reserved until validated dates and substantive change records exist.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>RelatedContent</code></dt><dd>Reserved until relationship records can resolve to public routes.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>Breadcrumbs</code> · <code>JsonLd</code></dt><dd>Trail and structured data; both derive from the registry.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Layout rhythm</h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt><code>--rhythm-row</code></dt><dd>Editorial list rows. Keeps scan density even across pages.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>--rhythm-block</code></dt><dd>Space between blocks inside one section.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>--rhythm-section</code></dt><dd>Space between major page sections.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Never hand-tune</dt><dd>If a composition needs different spacing, change the role — not the one page.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Style modules</h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt><code>.button</code></dt><dd>Variants: <code>--primary</code>, <code>--secondary</code>, <code>--poster</code>.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>HomeHero</code> · <code>PageHeader</code> · <code>CommercialHero</code> · <code>EntryHeader</code></dt><dd>Shared route and editorial openings.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>LoopField</code></dt><dd>The framed agent/human loop diagram used by Home and this gallery.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>ProofStrip</code> · <code>VerifiedClaims</code></dt><dd>Display-only evidence patterns fed by public-safe selectors.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>SignalList</code> · <code>ProcessDiagram</code> · <code>EntryPoints</code> · <code>CaseFeature</code> · <code>OutcomeColumns</code></dt><dd>Shared homepage and Brand Lab compositions.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>SectionHeading</code></dt><dd>Shared split or stacked section introduction with token-owned spacing.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>.prose</code> · <code>.evidence-note</code></dt><dd>Reading measure and proof blocks.</dd></div>
            <div><dt><code>.case-card</code> · <code>.cta-panel</code></dt><dd>Collection tiles and closing action plates.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

