    <section class="brand-lab__section" id="brand-recipes" aria-labelledby="brand-recipes-title">
      <div class="brand-lab__section-heading">
        <p class="brand-lab__index">17 / Recipes</p>
        <div><BrandHeading level={2} role="h3" id="brand-recipes-title">Ship a page without rediscovering the system</BrandHeading><p>Routes, canonical URLs, and navigation come from <code>src/config/routes.ts</code>. Start there, then assemble known modules.</p></div>
      </div>
      <ol class="brand-lab__recipe-steps">
        <li><span>01</span><strong>Register the route</strong><p>Add a <code>ROUTE_REGISTRY</code> entry with an <code>id</code>, path, <code>visibility</code>, gate, and navigation placement.</p></li>
        <li><span>02</span><strong>Choose the layout</strong><p>Pass <code>routeId</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, and <code>visibility</code> so canonical URLs and structured data stay derived.</p></li>
        <li><span>03</span><strong>Assemble known modules</strong><p>Use inventoried components and style modules; add new CSS only for a genuinely new responsibility.</p></li>
        <li><span>04</span><strong>Attach evidence</strong><p>Every claim, metric, or outcome needs an <code>EvidenceNote</code> source or it stays unpublished.</p></li>
        <li><span>05</span><strong>Verify</strong><p>Run <code>npm run check &amp;&amp; npm run build &amp;&amp; npm test &amp;&amp; npm run verify</code> before calling it done.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brand-lab__recipe-grid">
        <article>
          <span>Commercial page</span>
          <strong>Services, about, contact</strong>
          <p><code>CommercialLayout</code> + <code>.page-header</code> + <code>.prose</code> + <code>.cta-panel</code>. Pass <code>kind="webpage"</code> when the page is not a service.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Case study</span>
          <strong>Evidence-backed project</strong>
          <p><code>CaseStudyLayout</code> + <code>EntryHeader</code> + <code>.prose</code> + <code>EvidenceNote</code> + <code>RelatedContent</code>. Canonical stays <code>/case-studies/[slug]/</code>.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Resource</span>
          <strong>Guide or starter</strong>
          <p><code>BaseLayout</code> + <code>JsonLd</code> + <code>Breadcrumbs</code> + <code>EntryHeader</code> + <code>.prose</code>, driven by the validated content collection.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Collection hub</span>
          <strong>Index of entries</strong>
          <p><code>PageHeader</code> + <code>SectionHeading</code> + <code>CollectionCard</code> list. A hub advertises itself only when it has a public child.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <aside class="brand-lab__recipe-guard">
        <strong>Before adding anything new</strong>
        <p>If an existing module nearly fits, extend its variant instead of creating a parallel pattern. New routes, tokens, and components each add a boundary someone must maintain.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

        <section class="brand-lab__section" id="brand-governance" aria-labelledby="brand-governance-title">
      <div class="brand-lab__section-heading">
        <p class="brand-lab__index">18 / Governance</p>
        <div><BrandHeading level={2} role="h3" id="brand-governance-title">One working boundary</BrandHeading><p>The archive informs decisions. Production components and tokens own the website.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="brand-lab__governance">
